---
description: Shell and Python execution environment
globs:
alwaysApply: true
---

Execution environment rules (apply to ALL shell / tool invocations, not just Python files):

- ALWAYS run Python and any command that imports project dependencies inside the conda environment `modelops`.
- Prefix commands with `conda run -n modelops <cmd>` (preferred, non-interactive) or `source activate modelops && <cmd>`.
- Never fall back to `/usr/bin/python3`, Homebrew Python, `pip install --user`, or any ad-hoc interpreter.
- Do NOT search for a venv, `.venv`, `virtualenv`, or attempt to install missing packages into the base environment. If a package appears missing, assume it belongs in `modelops` and either use `conda run -n modelops pip install <pkg>` or ask before installing.
- This applies to one-off scripts, notebooks, data analysis, tests, and any `python`, `pip`, `pytest`, `dvc`, `mlflow`, or project CLI invocation.
